        "id": 1305927
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-01-25T17:25:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If we\u0027re still running all the tests in the same POSIX session, i.e. without resetting the EC, this shouldn\u0027t happen before every test. IRL, this device would only reset when the whole board power cycles. Our code wouldn\u0027t expect it to reset while the EC is running and might misbehave.\n\nThis is mostly true for PPCs and TCPCs and probably chargers where they are always part of the power path. The EC would only expect them to reset when it tells them to, if it even has the ability to reset them.",
      "revId": "ed5bf9d3daf341afb9e97d89031c3ce0d405fea4",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1cf32fb3_072aac1a",
        "filename": "zephyr/emul/emul_syv682x.c",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 344,
      "author": {
        "id": 1333748
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-01-25T17:49:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The issue is that there\u0027s no way for tests to keep track of the state of the full EC. Instead we should be resetting to some common state before each test and allowing each test to set up their own scenario.",
      "parentUuid": "fc1a5362_7f73bb81",
      "revId": "ed5bf9d3daf341afb9e97d89031c3ce0d405fea4",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
